---
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';
---

<Site
  title="Your feed, your choices"
  description="Explore category controls for your LinkedIn home feed in a free, synthetic demo. Development preview; live filtering is not yet available."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div>
      <h1>Your feed, your choices.</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        More of what you came for. Choose the categories you want to see, hide
        the ones you don’t, and keep the final say.
      </p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="button" href="/demo/">
          Try the synthetic demo
        </a>
        <a href="/how-it-works/">See how the rules work</a>
      </div>
      <p>No account. No API key. Just sample posts.</p>
    </div>
    <div
      class="sample-feed"
      aria-label="Illustrative feed rules, not live predictions"
    >
      <p>Synthetic feed preview</p>
      <article>
        <strong>A compiler launch with real benchmarks</strong>
        <p>
          A launch can also be useful technical content. Your “Always show” rule
          takes priority.
        </p>
        <span class="rule">Always show: Technical content</span>
      </article>
      <article>
        <strong>Hidden: Engagement bait</strong>
        <p>
          Hidden posts keep a reveal control. Change your mind whenever you
          like.
        </p>
        <a href="/demo/">Try hiding and revealing a sample</a>
      </article>
      <article>
        <strong>Something big is coming…</strong>
        <p>Not enough context? It stays visible.</p>
        <span class="rule">Visible: Uncertain classification</span>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="principles" aria-label="Your controls">
    <div>
      <h2>Choose by category</h2>
      <p>
        Job postings, referrals, technical content, product launches, and more.
        Every category starts visible.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h2>Protect what matters</h2>
      <p>
        “Always show” wins over a hidden category. “Show normally” leaves other
        rules in place.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h2>Keep an easy way back</h2>
      <p>
        Reveal a post, pause filtering, or withdraw consent. The intended
        behavior is to restore your feed.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="closing">
    <h2>Understand it before you connect it.</h2>
    <p>
      The demo runs entirely on fixed synthetic examples. Future live
      classification would send minimized post text to your selected provider
      and may incur API charges. No provider connection is available in this
      preview.
    </p>
    <a href="/privacy/">Read about data and privacy</a>
  </section>
</Site>
